@startuml
title Sequence diagram: coordinator reviews the request and asks for clarification
hide footbox
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center

' People work in the Web App, which calls the Backend API with their login token, so
' every call and its answer is two arrows: person <-> Web App, Web App <-> Backend API.
' Only the arrows to and from the Backend API and PostgreSQL are numbered, as in the
' draw.io and PDF versions.
' Starting the review notifies nobody and is optional: a submitted request can be decided
' directly. Asking a question needs the request to be under review. Each status change
' and its history entry are saved in one commit; the notification is saved after it, and
' its recipient's Web App fetches it later.

actor "Event\nCoordinator" as coordinator
actor "Event\nOrganiser" as organiser
participant "Web App\n(React)" as web
participant "Backend API" as api
database "PostgreSQL" as db

== Coordinator reviews the request (assigned to them; starting the review is optional) ==
coordinator -> web : Open the request
autonumber
web -> api : GET /api/events/requests/:reference
api --> web : The request record: status, equipment, decision
autonumber stop
web --> coordinator : Show the request

coordinator -> web : Start the review
autonumber resume
web -> api : POST /api/events/requests/:reference/review
api -> db : Status becomes under_review,\nadd a history entry
api --> web : The request, now under review
autonumber stop
web --> coordinator : Show the status

== Optional: the coordinator needs more information (the request must be under review) ==
opt Information is missing
  coordinator -> web : Ask for clarification
  autonumber resume
  web -> api : POST /api/events/requests/\n:reference/request-clarification
  api -> db : Status becomes\nawaiting_clarification, add\na history entry
  api -> db : Save notification: organiser,\nwith the question
  api --> web : The request, now awaiting clarification
  autonumber stop
  web --> coordinator : Show the status

  organiser -> web : Open notifications
  autonumber resume
  web -> api : GET /api/notifications
  api --> web : Your coordinator asked a question
  autonumber stop
  web --> organiser : Show notifications

  organiser -> web : Answer
  autonumber resume
  web -> api : POST /api/events/requests/:reference/resubmit
  api -> db : Status back to under_review,\nadd the answer to the history
  api -> db : Save notification: coordinator,\nwith the answer
  api --> web : The request, back under review
  autonumber stop
  web --> organiser : Show the status

  coordinator -> web : Open notifications
  autonumber resume
  web -> api : GET /api/notifications
  api --> web : The organiser answered, with the answer
  autonumber stop
  web --> coordinator : Show notifications
end
@enduml
